# Brenz messages

Source: `@docs/product/brenz-message-bank.md` and `@docs/architecture/brenz-architecture-domain.md` (Messages section).

## Voice rules
- Write in first person. No nickname.
- Aim sarcasm at the action, never at the person.
- Do not mention work, office or clothing.
- Talk about classes, consistency and training.
- Failure messages: acknowledge the fact, observe the habit, propose a small step.

## Logic rules
- Choose the state message once per state and day. It lasts the whole day.
- Rotate without repeating until the 5 of the state are exhausted. Store the used indexes.
- Water rotation: only avoid repeating the previous one of the same group.
- Priority when adding water: goal reached, half, add one glass.
- Half of the goal: with the user's goal (4 to 16), round up.
- Animated only because of water: show the goal-reached message.
- "Dropped below the goal": only if the state went down from animated to normal. Otherwise, "One glass less".
- (T) messages of normal: only if there is no class today.
- Water messages: about 4 s in the bubble, then the base message returns. They open the bubble even if it is closed.
- "No glasses at midday": after 12:00 local, with 0 glasses, once per day.
- "New user": only with no classes and only once.

## Keys and text
- Name keys `message.<group>.<n>`. Example: `message.state.animated.1`.
- Write each message in `en` and `es`.
- Replace the stage placeholder of the bank with `%1$@`. Pass the stage name (`stage.1.name`) as the argument.
- Test that every `MessageKey` exists in both languages.

## Forbidden
- Do not write the stage name by hand in a message.
- Do not use a nickname placeholder or the nickname in any message.
- Do not choose messages in the view or in the ViewModel.
- Do not store the rotation in Firestore.
